    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d434">

                <pb facs="0652" n="564" sameAs="frus:frus1892/pg564"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Blaine to Mr. Hirsch.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1892-04-25"><hi rendition="#italic">April 25,
                        1892</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 319.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge receipt of your No.
                    423 of 8th instant, and the statement which you inclose relative to the
                    continued tampering of the interior officials of Turkey with the consignments of
                    American books which have been stamped and sealed with the approval of the
                    Imperial Government. The Department must express its surprise that after your
                    frequently repeated protests these subordinates of the provinces are still
                    permitted to set at defiance the acts of the central Government.</p>
                <p>Your note of April the 8th last intimates to the Porte that damages will be
                    required.</p>
                <p>Approving your note, I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">James G. Blaine.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
